  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Request for Comments",
    "overview": "Every Redactor surface is set as a standards document. Redactor's placeholders already are citation keys, so the in-chat review is a References section, the settings page is a spec with a contents page, and the popup is a short memo with the same header block. Paper and ink, hairline rules, one text size, and a monospace voice reserved for the parts a document would set in mono: keys, masked values, header blocks, positions.\n\nThe layer sits on top of third-party AI chat apps, so it has to be recognisably Redactor while staying calm beside the host. It does that by refusing the rounded-card, blue-filled-button, soft-shadow vocabulary every extension ships, and by ranking text with weight and position instead of size. Density is a document's density: rows on rules, no boxes around groups, aligned columns.\n\nLight mode is paper ground with ink text; dark mode inverts to an ink ground with paper-toned text. Both modes follow `prefers-color-scheme` and carry the same roles.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Paper and ink ground; one accent for keys, one for the risky action, nothing else coloured.",
      "A single 14px text size; rank comes from weight (700, 600, 400) and position.",
      "Mono only for keys, masked values, header blocks, positions and leader values.",
      "Hairline rules separate rows; an ink rule closes the header block and opens the footer.",
      "Square-ish corners (3px controls, 4px sheets).",
      "Sized in px throughout (host pages shrink the root font; browser zoom still scales px)."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Keys-Only Rule",
        "body": "Citation blue marks keys and focus, never decoration and never a filled surface.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rubric Rule",
        "body": "Red appears only on the risky or blocking path. If an element is red, choosing it sends something unredacted or explains why that was stopped.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The One Size Rule",
        "body": "Prose and headings share 14px. Rank by weight and placement; do not add a larger display size.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Typewriter Rule",
        "body": "Mono is reserved for what a standards document sets in mono: keys, masked values, header blocks, positions, numbers in leaders. Never for prose or headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
